"view.ltephemeris.help"                     = "In the Long Time Ephemeris you can calculate planetary positions over any period at a chosen interval.\n\nEnter a start date and an end date. 'G' stands for the Gregorian calendar and 'J' for the Julian calendar.\n\nEnter the interval between rows in days and hours. At least one of these must be greater than zero.\n\nYou can specify whether you want geocentric or heliocentric positions, and whether to use the sidereal or tropical zodiac.\n\nChoose one of the available coordinates. If you have selected heliocentric positions, right ascension and declination are not available.\n\nChoose the display format: DMS (degrees, minutes, seconds) or Decimal (four decimal places).\n\nSelect one or more factors to calculate. Factors already active in your configuration are pre-selected.\n\nClick Calculate to start. A progress bar is shown for long calculations; you can cancel at any time.";
